// TEMPLATE (mechanical layer) — tb/{{ ip }}_dump.sv. The waveform dump for {{ ip }}, in its OWN
// top-level module (listed in filelist.f after tb/{{ ip }}_tb_top.sv), active only with +DUMP:
//     bash flow/scripts/xsim_flow.sh run ips/{{ ip }} <test> <seed> --plusargs +DUMP
//
// Why a separate top and not an `if ($test$plusargs("DUMP"))` inside {{ ip }}_tb_top: on Vivado
// xsim the mere PRESENCE of $dumpvars in the elaborated design stops code-toggle recording on
// some DUT nets, even when it never executes. xsim_flow.sh leaves this top out of the
// code-toggle snapshot, and run_regression.py refuses a toggle build whose tb top has a dump.
module {{ ip }}_dump;
    initial begin
        if ($test$plusargs("DUMP")) begin
            $dumpfile("{{ ip }}.vcd");
            $dumpvars(0, {{ ip }}_tb_top);
        end
    end
endmodule
